Offshore gaming platforms are being openly promoted on social media, while Indian skill gaming platforms have been banned under the #PROGA law.

The biggest question is: Why does this law seem to have little impact on offshore platforms, while Indian legal skill gaming platforms have been forced to shut down?

When legal Indian platforms are completely shut down, what alternatives are left for users other than turning to offshore platforms?

The government should reconsider its approach and focus on regulation, not prohibition. Indian skill gaming platforms should be allowed to operate under a strong regulatory framework with proper KYC, taxation, consumer protection and strict compliance.

At the same time, illegal offshore platforms must face strict enforcement action.

